          "config": {
            "title": "Notice the sentence relationship",
            "retryIncorrect": true,
            "slides": [
              {
                "id": "ielts-l0001-e04-rule",
                "type": "teaching-card",
                "chrome": { "header": { "progress": null } },
                "data": {
                  "mode": "rule",
                  "instruction": "Study the order before repairing the sentence.",
                  "title": "Put the action after the subject",
                  "markdown": "### A simple statement\nUse **subject + present-tense verb + object** with *I, you, we,* and *they*.\n\n- I eat rice.\n- We drink water.\n\n#### Check the relationship\nIn *I eat rice*, **I** is the subject, **eat** is the verb, and **rice** is the object. Start with a capital letter and finish with a full stop."
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "ielts-l0001-e04-correction",
                "type": "error-correction",
                "data": {
                  "instruction": "Correct the word order and punctuation.",
                  "mode": "sentence-correction",
                  "category": "subject–verb–object order",
                  "original": "i rice eat",
                  "answers": ["I eat rice."],
                  "explanation": "Place the verb after the subject and the object after the verb. Use capital I and a final full stop."
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "ielts-l0001-e04-summary",
                "type": "summary",
                "terminal": true,
                "data": {
                  "aggregationMode": "first-attempts",
                  "title": "You can build a simple subject–verb–object statement"
                },
                "chrome": {
                  "footer": {
                    "primary": { "id": "finish", "label": "Finish", "behavior": "emit" },
                    "secondary": false
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
